      "problem": "Evaluate $\\int (2{x}^{4}+4x){e}^{3x}\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "For this integral, we choose $u=2{x}^{4}+4x$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{3x}.$ Filling in our table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2{x}^{4}+4x$ | ${e}^{3x}$ |  |  |\n| $8{x}^{3}+4$ | $\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{(2{x}^{4}+4x){e}^{3x}}{3}$ |\n| $24{x}^{2}$ | $\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{(8{x}^{3}+4){e}^{3x}}{9}$ |\n| $48x$ | $\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{27}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{8{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{9}$ |\n| $48$ | $\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{81}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{16x{e}^{3x}}{27}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{243}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{16{e}^{3x}}{81}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{x}^{4}+4x){e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{81}(27(2{x}^{4}+4x)-9(8{x}^{3}+4)+9(8{x}^{2})-3(16x)+16)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{81}(54{x}^{4}-72{x}^{3}+72{x}^{2}+60x-20)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{3x}}{81}(27{x}^{4}-36{x}^{3}+36{x}^{2}+30x-10)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
